Local review patch: free pruned CPU list on successful cpu-map handoff
Base: m1n1 4184923ffb2dff079b384d6a32cc02142aa14572, after 0001
Provenance: AI-assisted project work; not submitted upstream.

The normal cpu-map path returned without releasing the temporary list used
while pruning dead CPUs.  The missing-cpu-map path already frees it.

---
 src/kboot.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -742,6 +742,7 @@ static int dt_set_cpus(void)
     if ((cluster_node < 0) && (cluster_node != -FDT_ERR_NOTFOUND))
         bail_cleanup("FDT: Error iterating through CPU clusters\n");
 
+    free(pruned_phandles);
     return 0;
 
 err:
